// Nova Nacao: linha de missoes de Portugal
POR_Line
{
For the Glory of the Crown
}

POR_Line.1
{
The Governor-General of the Portuguese colonies, Francisco Barreto de Meneses, received me coldly but gave me a commission: pirates are taking our merchantmen between Cumaná and Trinidad, always knowing when they sail. I must find the Corvo Negro in the waters of Trinidad and sink her, and report only to him.
}

POR_Line.f
{
I left the area before the fight was over. The enemy is still there; I must go back and finish the job.
}

POR_Line.2
{
The Corvo Negro is no more. Her captain, Bento Malheiro, was Portuguese, from Recife. Before he died he said something strange: the pirates always know the day our ships leave Cumaná, 'and Spaniards don't know that kind of thing'. Among his things: Spanish doubloons and a list of our sailing dates. I must report to the Governor-General in Caracas.
}

POR_Line.3
{
Promoted to Captain. The governor kept the list and told me to keep quiet. Now I must find Tomé Ferraz, a Portuguese merchant in the tavern of Willemstad, on Curaçao. He is said to be unfriendly.
}

POR_Line.4
{
Tomé Ferraz only opened up when I told him about Malheiro. A Spanish courier, the Santa Clara, brings the pirates' pay from Havana and anchors off Aruba. I must intercept her. Tomé warned me to think hard before handing the letters to anyone.
}

POR_Line.5
{
The Santa Clara has been taken. From the half-burnt letters I could read: gold for every Portuguese ship taken in the Caribbean, raids on the sugar fleets of Pernambuco and Bahia, and a mention of 'our friend in Caracas'. I must report to the Governor-General.
}

POR_Line.6
{
The governor dismissed 'our friend in Caracas' as just another spy. Now I must protect the fluyt Desterro, bringing sugar from Pernambuco, when she arrives at Cumaná. How does he know the pirates will strike there?
}

POR_Line.7a
{
The pirates off Cumaná have been beaten and the Desterro is safe. Her captain, Amaro Teles, wants to buy me a drink in the tavern of Cumaná.
}

POR_Line.7
{
Amaro Teles changed course on purpose this voyage. Only the Governor-General's office knew his new route, and the pirates were waiting for him anyway. I must report to the governor... carefully.
}

POR_Line.7b
{
The pirates off Cumaná have been beaten, but the Desterro went down. I must report to the Governor-General.
}

POR_Line.8
{
Promoted to Capitão-Mor. The governor wants me to destroy the squadron of Gaspar Roiz, 'Iron Hand', off the Cayman Islands. He says Roiz 'has grown greedy', and he wants any papers found on board brought straight to him.
}

POR_Line.9
{
Iron Hand's squadron is destroyed. Roiz said the governor sent me after him only because he had asked for a bigger share. In his strongbox I found a ledger: cargoes taken from Portuguese ships, all sold to a merchant in Caracas, Simão Godinho, 'by order of the Palace'. I must decide what to tell the governor.
}

POR_Line.9b
{
Iron Hand's squadron is at the bottom of the sea, and Gaspar Roiz with it. Among the floating wreckage my men fished out a sealed strongbox. Inside was a ledger: cargoes taken from Portuguese ships, all sold to a merchant in Caracas, Simão Godinho, 'by order of the Palace'. I must decide what to tell the governor.
}

POR_Line.10
{
Promoted to Admiral. The governor called me 'a most useful instrument'. I have Simão Godinho's name; I must find him in the tavern of Caracas.
}

POR_Line.11
{
Godinho broke when I mentioned the governor: the stolen goods went to the governor's warehouses, under his own seal. His secretary, Lourenço Viegas, copied every contract and fled to Cumaná. I must find him in the tavern there.
}

POR_Line.12
{
The truth at last. Barreto made a pact with a Spanish agent in Havana: Spain pays the pirates, the pirates hand over the cargoes, and the governor sells them and shares the profit. And I was the broom he used to sweep away the pirates who demanded too much. Lourenço gave me the copies of the contracts. The Crown's Desembargador, Dom Álvaro de Sousa Coutinho, is arriving by ship, and Barreto will try to stop him. I must put to sea off Cumaná and protect his ship, then deliver the copies to him in the residence of Cumaná.
}

POR_Line.13
{
Killers under the Spanish flag were waiting off Cumaná for the Desembargador's ship. They are gone, and Dom Álvaro has landed. He is waiting for me in the residence of Cumaná.
}

POR_Line.14
{
Dom Álvaro read the contracts and named me General. But Barreto de Meneses has fled Caracas aboard his galleon, the São Miguel. I must intercept him in the waters of Caracas, alive if possible.
}

POR_Line.15
{
Barreto de Meneses surrendered. He admitted he used me from the first day. I must take him to Dom Álvaro in the residence of Cumaná.
}

POR_Line.15b
{
The São Miguel went down, and Barreto de Meneses with her. I must take the news to Dom Álvaro in the residence of Cumaná.
}

POR_Line.16
{
The pirate network is broken and the traitor has been brought to justice. By order of His Majesty Dom Afonso VI, I am now the Governor-General of the Portuguese colonies of the Caribbean. Every month a tenth of each Portuguese colony's profit goes to the treasury in Caracas, where Lourenço Viegas keeps my accounts.
}

POR_Line.2b
{
The Corvo Negro went down with her captain. My men pulled a half-drowned pirate out of the water: the captain was Bento Malheiro, a Portuguese from Recife, and he 'always knew the day our ships leave Cumaná'. The captain's chest floated free of the wreck: Spanish doubloons and a list of our sailing dates. I must report to the Governor-General in Caracas.
}

POR_Line.5b
{
The Santa Clara went to the bottom, but her oilcloth mail bag floated among the wreckage. From the soaked letters I could read: gold for every Portuguese ship taken in the Caribbean, raids on the sugar fleets of Pernambuco and Bahia, and a mention of 'our friend in Caracas'. I must report to the Governor-General.
}

// Nova Nacao: despachos do Governador-Geral
POR_Orders
{
Governor-General's Dispatches
}

POR_Orders.hunt
{
Lourenço Viegas passed me a dispatch: a pirate is taking our coasters in the waters of @<sPlace>. The treasury will pay @<sMoney> once she is at the bottom. There is no deadline, and if I change my mind I only need to tell Lourenço.
}

POR_Orders.smug
{
Lourenço Viegas passed me a dispatch: smugglers are cheating the Crown of its duties in the waters of @<sPlace>. The customs house will pay @<sMoney>, and their cargo is mine. There is no deadline, and if I change my mind I only need to tell Lourenço.
}

POR_Orders.fleet
{
Spanish privateers are waiting for part of the Brazil fleet in the waters of @<sPlace>. If I get there before the fleet reaches port, the treasury will pay @<sMoney> and the Crown's share of the cargo will be larger.
}

POR_Orders.done
{
The job is done. @<sMoney> was deposited in the treasury at the seat of government.
}

POR_Orders.done_lost_escort
{
The pirates are gone, but the desembargador's ship went down with him. Half the reward, @<sMoney>, was deposited in the treasury.
}

POR_Orders.done_loss
{
The privateers are gone, but we lost ships of the fleet. Half the reward, @<sMoney>, was deposited in the treasury.
}

POR_Orders.flee
{
I left those waters before the fight was over. The enemy is still there.
}

POR_Orders.cancel
{
I told Lourenço to give this dispatch to someone else. No one asked questions.
}

POR_Orders.fleet_gone
{
The Brazil fleet's voyage ended before I reached the privateers. The dispatch no longer matters.
}

POR_Orders.priv
{
Lourenço Viegas passed me a dispatch: @<sName>, a Spanish privateer, is hunting Portuguese ships in the waters of @<sPlace>. The treasury will pay @<sMoney> for him. There is no deadline.
}

POR_Orders.escort
{
A desembargador's ship will pass through the waters of @<sPlace>, and pirates are waiting for it. I must meet it there and see that it arrives safely. The treasury will pay @<sMoney>. There is no deadline.
}

POR_Orders.supply
{
The garrison of @<sPlace> needs @<sQty> of @<sGood>. I must bring them to Lourenço Viegas; the treasury will pay @<sMoney>. There is no deadline.
}

POR_Orders.supplied
{
I delivered the supplies to the garrison. @<sMoney> was deposited in the treasury.
}
#endreplace
